-- PLC Intelligence demo seed
-- Replacement for data/seed.sql
-- Generated 2026-08-18
--
-- PURPOSE
-- Four intentionally different PLC scenarios support a clear guided workflow:
--
-- 1) 3rd Grade PLC
--    Current focus: Mathematics / 3.NF.2
--    Story: CFA evidence is available and the team should Analyze Data & Evidence of Learning.
--    Signal: locating non-unit fractions on a number line is intentionally the weakest component skill.
--
-- 2) 5th Grade PLC
--    Current focus: English Language Arts / 5.R.6
--    Story: a new PLC cycle is beginning. The team should Determine Essential Learning Targets.
--    No current-cycle assessment evidence is seeded.
--
-- 3) Middle School Math PLC
--    Current focus: Grade 7 proportional relationships / 7.RP.2
--    Story: the team has responded to initial evidence and has improved from the first measure.
--    The next instructional move is reassessment/progress monitoring.
--
-- 4) Middle School Science PLC
--    Current focus: Grade 8 matter/thermal energy / SCI.8.1.5
--    Story: three measures show substantial progress over time, but one component skill remains weaker.
--    The next PLC move is Collaborative Inquiry.
--
-- ELEMENTARY TEAM MODEL
-- The 3rd Grade PLC and 5th Grade PLC are grade-level teams. The same teachers/students
-- are seeded into multiple subject sections. The CURRENT plc_teams schema still requires
-- one subject value, so each elementary team's subject column is temporarily set to the
-- subject of its current cycle. This should be relaxed when multi-subject PLC support is
-- added to the schema/repositories.
--
-- COMPONENT SKILL COMPATIBILITY
-- The current app schema/repositories still use the table/column names
-- standard_core_ideas/core_idea_id. This seed stores COMPONENT SKILLS in that existing
-- structure so it runs against the current application. Rename the schema objects later
-- as part of the Core Idea -> Component Skill refactor.
--
-- DATA VOLUME
-- * 4 PLC teams
-- * 3 teachers per team
-- * 25 students per teacher section (75 students per team)
-- * elementary teachers have both Math and ELA sections
-- * 4 component skills per current essential standard
-- * 12 CFA questions per assessed standard (3 questions per component skill)
-- * student-level results are deliberately engineered, not random
--
-- IMPORTANT
-- Delete data/plc_demo.db before rebuilding so the replacement seed is applied cleanly.
-- services/database.py runs the weekly schema before this seed, so the week tables below
-- are available. term1_2026_27_seed.sql can safely run afterward because it uses
-- INSERT OR IGNORE for the same term/week rows.

